摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"The SEO audit toolkit built for DeepSeek Harness (DSH) — runs locally, no Claude Code, no API key required. Self-contained port of claude-seo v2.2.5: 53 Python scripts + 24 sub-skills + 18 agents, weighted score, gated fan-out, schema.org, E-E-A-T, GBP, GEO/AI Overviews.","id":"gh:1350874403","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"seo-toolkit","slug":"Haniubub/seo-toolkit","topics":["claude-code","claude-skills","deep-seek-plugin","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","dsh-skill","eeat","geo","local-seo","schema-org","seo","seo-audit","seo-automation","seo-optimization","seo-tools","technical-seo"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"The SEO audit toolkit built for DeepSeek Harness (DSH) — runs locally, no Claude Code, no API key re"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"quired. Self-contained port of claude-seo v2.2.5: 53 Python scripts + 24 sub-skills + 18 agents, wei"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"ghted score, gated fan-out, schema.org, E-E-A-T, GBP, GEO/AI Overviews."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# seo-audit — the DSH-native SEO audit toolkit for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> **Status:** production-ready · **v1.0.0**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"A production-grade SEO audit toolkit **built for DeepSeek Harness (DSH)** that runs a\nfull, weighted"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" technical, content, schema and local audit on any website — **self-contained\nand strictly local**: "},{"id":"p5s3","text":"no Claude Code, no plugin marketplace, no third-party SaaS, no\nper-domain pricing, and **no API key "},{"id":"p5s4","text":"required for the core audit**. It executes as a\nplain CLI + agent library in the DeepSeek Harness en"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"vironment and works out of the box."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Unlike SEO skills bound to Claude Code, seo-audit is **DSH-native**: you run it in the\nharness you a"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"lready use, with nothing leaving your machine."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Built for **local SEO**, **technical SEO**, **schema.org**, **E-E-A-T**, **GEO / AI Overviews**,\n**G"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"oogle Business Profile (GBP)**, **on-page & content** audits across any industry."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"It combines **deterministic measurement** (own Python specialists + 53 curated\nscripts) with **LLM-d"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"riven judgment** (24 sub-skills + 18 specialist agents), and\nsynthesises everything into one weighte"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"d, prioritised report."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The audit logic is anchored in primary-source Google guidance and this is a native,\nself-contained p"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ort of the MIT toolkit\nAgriciDaniel/claude-seo v2.2.5 —\nsee Attribution & License."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Quick answer"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**seo-audit is a free, local SEO audit toolkit for DeepSeek Harness (DSH).** You run\none command (`."},{"id":"p11s2","text":"/seo audit <url>`) and get a weighted, prioritised action plan covering\ntechnical SEO, on-page, sche"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ma/JSON-LD, E-E-A-T, GEO/AI Overviews, Local/GBP, backlinks,\ne-commerce, sitemap, image SEO, content"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" briefs, keyword clustering, drift tracking and\nGoogle APIs (PSI/CrUX/GSC). It runs on your own mach"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"ine — **no per-domain pricing, no\nSaaS, and no API key required for the core audit**. Measurement (5"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"3 Python scripts +\n`lib/`) is deterministic; judgment (24 sub-skills + 18 agents, e.g. E-E-A-T, GEO/"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"AIO,\nGBP) is LLM-driven. Every recommendation carries the four claude-seo fields:\n**Observation → De"},{"id":"p11s8","text":"pendency → Failure signal → Early indicator.**"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**Top use cases:** auditing a website's search visibility, technical SEO, schema markup,\ncontent/E-E"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"-A-T, local SEO or Google Business Profile, GEO/AI-Overview readiness, Core\nWeb Vitals, sitemap/href"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"lang, keyword clustering, content briefs and drift tracking."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## FAQ"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Is seo-audit free?\nYes. It's MIT-licensed and runs locally. The core audit needs **no API key, n"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"o account,\nno domain pricing** — only Python 3.10+, `requests`, `beautifulsoup4`, `lxml` and\nPlaywri"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ght (installed by `./setup.sh` into a workspace-local `pylibs/`)."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### Does it need Claude Code or a subscription?\nNo. seo-audit is a self-contained port of claude-seo"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" and runs standalone. It needs **no\nClaude Code, no plugin marketplace and no third-party SaaS**."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Does it work without a Google API key?\nThe core audit works fully without any key. Google APIs ("},{"id":"p16s2","text":"PageSpeed, CrUX, GSC, GA4),\nDataForSEO, Firecrawl, Ahrefs, Bing and Banana are ported but only activ"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ate once you\nsupply their own credentials — otherwise they degrade gracefully."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### How does it differ from claude-seo?\nIt's a native, self-contained port of claude-seo v2.2.5 (MIT"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"-compatible), with the same\nweighted score (Technical 22% · Content 23% · On-Page 20% · Schema 10% ·"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" Performance\n10% · AI-Readiness 10% · Images 5%) and the same gated multi-agent fan-out, but it runs"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"\nentirely in your own environment."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### What are the four claude-seo fields?\nEvery recommendation ships with **Observation → Dependency "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"→ Failure signal → Early\nindicator**: field 2 sets the execution order, field 3 tells you how you'd "},{"id":"p18s3","text":"know it\nworked, field 4 is the leading signal to watch."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"A full audit is split into two layers:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Layer | What it is | How it runs |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| **Measurement** | 5 Python specialists + 53 curated scripts | `./seo <command>` |\n| **Judgment** |"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" 24 sub-skills + 18 agent prompts (E-E-A-T, GEO/AIO, Local/GBP, SXO, …) | Agent executes via `subage"},{"id":"p22s3","text":" 18 agent prompts (E-E-A-T, GEO/AIO, Local/GBP, SXO, …) | Agent executes via `subagent`/`workflow` |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Every recommendation carries the four claude-seo fields:\n**Observation → Dependency → Failure signal"},{"id":"p23s2","text":" → Early indicator.**"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Example output"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"A sample of the top recommendations an audit produces, with their four fields.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"**Weighted SEO Health Score** (claude-seo parity): Technical 22% · Content 23%\n· On-Page 20% · Schem"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"a 10% · Performance 10% · AI-Readiness 10% · Images 5%."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"**Sandbox-safe runtime:** workspace-local `pylibs/` (pinned to known-good\n`lxml==5.4.0`, `requests=="},{"id":"p29s2","text":"2.32.5`, `playwright==1.55.0`) and `browsers/`."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- Python 3.10+ on macOS/Linux\n- `requests`, `beautifulsoup4`, `lxml`, `playwright` (see `requirement"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"n 3.10+ on macOS/Linux\n- `requests`, `beautifulsoup4`, `lxml`, `playwright` (see `requirements.txt`)"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Key-gated features"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"Google APIs (PageSpeed, CrUX, GSC, GA4), DataForSEO, Firecrawl, Ahrefs, Bing and\nBanana are **ported"},{"id":"p33s2","text":" but require their own credentials**. Without them the core\nmeasurement still works fully."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Security & credentials"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Your API keys are read from **environment variables** at runtime\n(`os.environ.get(...)`) — nothing i"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"s stored in the repo or in a config file that\ngets committed. A few best practices:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"- Use **scoped, temporary keys** for audits (a throwaway token or a limited-key\ncredential with only"},{"id":"p36s2","text":" the permissions you need).\n- **Delete the key when you're done** — after the audit, revoke/remove i"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"t. Don't\nleave it sitting in your shell profile.\n- Keys are redacted from any printed or saved outpu"},{"id":"p36s4","text":"t, but treat them as live\nsecrets regardless: never paste a real key into a log, an issue, or a shar"},{"id":"p36s5","text":"ed\nconfig.\n- The core audit needs **no key at all** — credentials only unlock the optional\nGoogle/Da"},{"id":"p36s6","text":"taForSEO/Firecrawl/Ahrefs/Bing data."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
